 "technique": [
  {
   "text": "This procedure may reduce speed below the manoeuvring speed for the current configuration, which is acceptable if the speed stays above VLS. Reduce speed and configure preferably with wings level.",
   "applies_to": [
    "all"
   ],
   "refs": [
    {
     "book": "FCTM",
     "code": "PR-AEP-F_CTL",
     "page": "P 2/6",
     "pdf": 429
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "text": "Assuming VLS is displayed, VAPP should be close to VLS + wind correction, because this speed is computed from the current slat/flap position. VAPP can be lower than VLS: then disconnect the A/THR above VLS when reducing to VAPP.",
   "applies_to": [
    "all"
   ],
   "refs": [
    {
     "book": "FCTM",
     "code": "PR-AEP-F_CTL",
     "page": "P 2/6",
     "pdf": 429
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "text": "The AP may be used down to 500 ft AGL. It is not tuned for abnormal configurations: monitor it.",
   "applies_to": [
    "all"
   ],
   "refs": [
    {
     "book": "FCTM",
     "code": "PR-AEP-F_CTL",
     "page": "P 2/6",
     "pdf": 429
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "text": "In the arrival briefing, emphasize tail strike awareness, the go-around configuration, any deviation from standard callout, the speeds after a missed approach, and selected speed for acceleration at the acceleration altitude.",
   "applies_to": [
    "all"
   ],
   "refs": [
    {
     "book": "FCTM",
     "code": "PR-AEP-F_CTL",
     "page": "P 2/6",
     "pdf": 429
    }
   ]
  }
 ],
